(CHAPTER 1: ADVANCED SQL & WINDOW ANALYTICS \(Page 1\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 1: Advanced SQL · Section 1.1 · Page 1]) Tj T*
(SQL is the cornerstone of enterprise data retrieval and analytics.) Tj T*
(Relational Joins combine tables horizontally on predicate keys. A Left Outer Join) Tj T*
(preserves all records from the left table regardless of matching records in the right) Tj T*
(table, populating unmatched right columns with NULL.) Tj T*
(Set Operations combine queries vertically:) Tj T*
(- UNION merges row sets and runs an implicit DISTINCT sort to eliminate duplicate) Tj T*
(tuples.) Tj T*
(- UNION ALL appends row sets directly without deduplication, preserving cardinality) Tj T*
(and executing with superior performance and lower memory overhead.) Tj T*
(- INTERSECT returns rows present in both queries; EXCEPT \(or MINUS\) returns rows) Tj T*
(present in the first query but absent in the second.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 1: Advanced SQL · Section 1.2 · Page 1]) Tj T*
(Window \(Analytic\) Functions compute calculations across a set of table rows related to) Tj T*
(the current row without collapsing the rows into a single summary output:) Tj T*
(Syntax: FUNCTION\(\) OVER \(PARTITION BY partition_col ORDER BY sort_col ROWS BETWEEN ...) Tj T*
(AND ...\)) Tj T*
(Ranking Differences:) Tj T*
(- ROW_NUMBER\(\): Assigns a unique sequential integer \(1, 2, 3, 4\) to every row) Tj T*
(regardless of ties.) Tj T*
(- RANK\(\): Assigns the same rank to identical values, but skips subsequent rank numbers) Tj T*
(\(e.g., ties at 2 result in 1, 2, 2, 4\).) Tj T*
(- DENSE_RANK\(\): Assigns the same rank to identical values without skipping numbers) Tj T*
(\(e.g., 1, 2, 2, 3\).) Tj T*
(Sliding Window Frames \(e.g., ROWS BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW\) compute moving) Tj T*
(averages and rolling sums over temporal partitions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 1: Advanced SQL · Section 1.3 · Page 1]) Tj T*
(Common Table Expressions \(CTEs\) define temporary named result sets using the WITH) Tj T*
(keyword:) Tj T*
(WITH RegionalSales AS \(SELECT region, SUM\(amount\) AS total FROM sales GROUP BY region\)) Tj T*
(CTEs improve modularity and readability compared to nested subqueries. A Recursive CTE) Tj T*
(references itself to traverse hierarchical data structures \(such as organizational) Tj T*
(management charts or bill-of-materials trees\) until a termination condition is met.) Tj T*
ET
