(CHAPTER 2: DATA WAREHOUSING & KIMBALL DIMENSIONAL MODELING \(Page 2\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 2: Data Warehousing · Section 2.1 · Page 2]) Tj T*
(Enterprise data architectures distinguish between OLTP and OLAP systems:) Tj T*
(- Online Transaction Processing \(OLTP\): Optimized for rapid, atomic) Tj T*
(insert/update/delete operations. Data is normalized to 3rd Normal Form \(3NF\) to) Tj T*
(eliminate redundant write anomalies and ensure ACID compliance.) Tj T*
(- Online Analytical Processing \(OLAP\): Optimized for complex analytical aggregations) Tj T*
(and historical reporting. Data is denormalized into multidimensional schemas \(Star or) Tj T*
(Snowflake\) to minimize expensive multi-table joins.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 2: Data Warehousing · Section 2.2 · Page 2]) Tj T*
(Kimball Dimensional Modeling organizes analytical data into two fundamental) Tj T*
(structures:) Tj T*
(1. Fact Tables: Store numeric measurements produced by business events \(e.g.,) Tj T*
(FactSales, FactWebsiteClicks\). Fact measures are classified as:) Tj T*
(   - Additive: Can be summed across all dimensions \(e.g., sales revenue, units sold\).) Tj T*
(   - Semi-Additive: Can be summed across some dimensions but not time \(e.g., bank) Tj T*
(account balances, inventory headcount\).) Tj T*
(   - Non-Additive: Cannot be summed across any dimension \(e.g., unit price, profit) Tj T*
(ratios\).) Tj T*
(2. Dimension Tables: Store textual context and business attributes \(e.g., DimCustomer,) Tj T*
(DimStore, DimDate\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 2: Data Warehousing · Section 2.3 · Page 2]) Tj T*
(Slowly Changing Dimensions \(SCD\) manage attribute modifications over time:) Tj T*
(- SCD Type 1: Overwrites existing attribute values with new data. Historical context) Tj T*
(is lost, but schema remains simple.) Tj T*
(- SCD Type 2: Preserves complete historical accuracy by creating a new dimension row) Tj T*
(whenever an attribute changes. Each row contains a surrogate primary key, the natural) Tj T*
(business key, Effective Start Date, Effective End Date, and a Current Active Flag) Tj T*
(\(IsCurrent = 1\).) Tj T*
(- SCD Type 3: Tracks previous values by adding a dedicated "Previous Attribute" column) Tj T*
(in the same row.) Tj T*
ET
