(CHAPTER 3: BUSINESS METRICS & UNIT ECONOMICS \(Page 3\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 3: Business Metrics · Section 3.1 · Page 3]) Tj T*
(Data analysts translate raw database records into strategic business performance) Tj T*
(metrics:) Tj T*
(- Customer Acquisition Cost \(CAC\): Total sales & marketing spend over a defined period) Tj T*
(divided by the number of new customers acquired: CAC = Total Marketing & Sales Costs /) Tj T*
(New Customers Acquired.) Tj T*
(- Customer Lifetime Value \(CLV / LTV\): Projected net gross margin contribution of a) Tj T*
(customer over their entire relationship:) Tj T*
(  LTV = \(Average Order Value * Purchase Frequency * Gross Margin %\) / Churn Rate.) Tj T*
(  Healthy SaaS and subscription business models target an LTV:CAC ratio of at least) Tj T*
(3:1.) Tj T*
(- Churn Rate: Percentage of customers or recurring revenue lost during a specific) Tj T*
(interval:) Tj T*
(  Customer Churn = \(Customers Lost during Period\) / \(Customers at Start of Period\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 3: Business Metrics · Section 3.2 · Page 3]) Tj T*
(Revenue and Cohort Analysis:) Tj T*
(- Monthly Recurring Revenue \(MRR\): Predictable subscription revenue normalized to a) Tj T*
(monthly interval.) Tj T*
(- Net Revenue Retention \(NRR\): Measures the percentage of recurring revenue retained) Tj T*
(from existing customers over a period, incorporating expansions \(upsells, cross-sells\)) Tj T*
(minus downgrades and cancellations:) Tj T*
(  NRR = \(Starting MRR + Expansion MRR - Contraction MRR - Churn MRR\) / Starting MRR *) Tj T*
(100.) Tj T*
(  An NRR > 100% indicates that expansion revenue outpaces churn, yielding organic) Tj T*
(company growth without acquiring a single new customer.) Tj T*
(- Cohort Retention Curves plot customer retention percentage over progressive months) Tj T*
(grouped by signup month, isolating product changes from acquisition marketing spikes.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
